    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded.\n\n**Summary: 8 PASS / 11 FAIL**\n\nPassing: search & filtering (FT-1), model detail navigation (FT-2), node dragging (FT-3), template library browsing (FT-6), scenario switching (FT-9), live coverage updates (IX-13), the directed weighted graph presentation (CT-15), and the risk-gap warning/alert behavior (CT-17, CT-18).\n\nThe failures cluster around three root defects:\n\n1. **The graph is a write-only control.** Level, weight and enabled-state edits update the summary analysis but never re-render the node — displayed level/weight/toggle/Gap/Critical indicators stay frozen at the initial values (FT-4, FT-5, IX-20, CT-16).\n2. **Edits do not accumulate.** Each edit is applied to the pristine model rather than the current state, so a second edit silently reverts the first, and a disabled competency can never be re-enabled (FT-5, IX-20).\n3. **Persistence and simulation wiring are incomplete.** Save shows a success toast but writes nothing (FT-11), \"Save Current\" offers no name/description and there is no My Templates collection (FT-8), applying a template leaves the old graph in place (FT-7), the initially selected scenario loads with empty defaults so running it is a no-op (IX-19), and the two adjustment sliders in each category overwrite each other with NaN, producing \"Coverage NaN%\" / \"Avg Level NaN\" and out-of-range weights (FT-10, CS-12)."
